  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two long parallel wires P and Q are a distance d apart. They each carry a current.</p>\n<p>A magnetic force per unit length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> acts on P due to Q.</p>\n<p>The distance between the wires is increased to 2d and the current in Q is decreased to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{I}{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the magnetic force per unit length that acts on P due to Q after the changes?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{8}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{4}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
